'''
There are 2 things we maintain:

partition order
every element in left heap <= every element in right heap
size balance
the heaps should be almost equal in size

Without the size rule, the partition alone is not enough to get the median.
'''

#How many elements should go in each heap?
'''
If n is even
Both heaps should have the same number of elements.
So:

left heap size = n/2
right heap size = n/2



If n is odd
One heap must have one extra element.

Usually we choose:

left heap size = n//2 + 1
right heap size = n//2

So left heap has one extra.


We maintain:

len(left) == len(right)
or
len(left) == len(right) + 1



So final computation rule is
even → (-left[0] + right[0]) / 2
odd → -left[0]
'''